<section class="section faq-section" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
  <div class="container faq-list">

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I need an architect?</summary>
      <p>Some projects require a licensed architect, but many remodels, additions, ADUs, and tenant improvements can be handled by an experienced building designer with the right consultant support.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can you help with permits?</summary>
      <p>Yes. ABC Design prepares permit-focused plans and helps coordinate responses during city review.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do you work with engineers?</summary>
      <p>Yes. When structural, civil, energy, or other consultant input is needed, Rick can coordinate the plan set requirements with those professionals.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How long does the design process take?</summary>
      <p>Timing depends on scope, site conditions, consultant needs, and jurisdiction review. Smaller projects can move quickly, while complex projects need more coordination.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What areas do you serve?</summary>
      <p>ABC Design serves San Diego County.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do you work on commercial projects?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Commercial work can include tenant improvements, restaurants, retail spaces, offices, and other permit plan needs.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do you provide project management?</summary>
      <p>ABC Design focuses on building design, drawings, permit plans, and related coordination. Full construction project management is typically handled separately.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do you build the projects you design?</summary>
      <p>No. ABC Design does not act as the builder. Rick can help prepare drawings that owners and contractors can use for bidding, permitting, and construction planning.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
